cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
title: "Experimentally mapped aggregation-critical protein regions, with circularity, prediction-concordance and training-set-contamination labels"
abstract: >-
  A hand-curated set of protein regions shown experimentally to be required for,
  or to constitute the core of, protein aggregation. Every row was established by
  opening the source paper and checking the claim against it. Each region carries
  the construct that established it, whether a predictor was in its discovery
  path (circularity), and whether experiment and prediction agree (stratum).
type: dataset
version: 1.4.0
authors:
  - family-names: "Mercier des Rochettes"
    given-names: "Bertrand"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-1145-1881"
    email: "contact@quantum-proteins.ai"
    affiliation: "Quantum Proteins AI, Cergy-Pontoise, France"
# Co-authors: NONE. Settled by the author 16 Nov 2026, asked and answered rather
# than assumed. Sole authorship is deliberate, not an oversight.
# Kept in step with .zenodo.json and with the Zenodo record itself. At v1.0.0 these three
# lists had drifted apart: this file carried 6 keywords, the record 8. Two were added for
# 1.1.0 for the CPAD check, and in the MANUAL deposit route they must be typed into the
# form -- .zenodo.json is not read by it.
keywords:
  - protein aggregation
  - amyloid
  - benchmark dataset
  - aggregation prediction
  - circularity
  - training set contamination
  - CPAD
  - curated dataset
  - TRIOBP-1
  - DISC1
# DECIDED by the author, 16 Nov 2026. Full legal code is in LICENSE.
# CC-BY-4.0 over CC0 because the value of this dataset is curatorial: the
# provenance, the circularity calls and the stratum labels are the work, and
# attribution is what makes a reader go back and check them. CC0 would maximise
# reuse but detach the rows from the reasoning that justifies them.
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/quantumproteinsai/mentalillness"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24290697"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24290697"
    description: "Concept DOI: always resolves to the latest version. Once v1.1.0 is published, its own version DOI is the one to cite for a specific analysis."
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24339193"
    description: "Version DOI of v1.3.0, the previous release. v1.4.0 supersedes it: v1.3.0 has no structure column, so it cannot say which deposited fibril structure a row's ordered core comes from, nor which rows have none at all."
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24337561"
    description: "Version DOI of v1.2.0, the previous release. v1.3.0 supersedes it: v1.2.0 carries seven rows at stratum PENDING whose labels this version assigns from the legacy predictor run, and it lacks the stratum_assignment column recording which labels were assigned blind and which were not."
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24306057"
    description: "Version DOI of v1.1.0, the previous release. v1.2.0 supersedes it: v1.1.0 holds 17 rows against this version's 21, lacking ANXA11 39-74, TMEM106B 120-254, glycinin G4 164-190 and the DISC1 interval split into the two sub-intervals its source tested. The deposited v1.1.0 copy of THIS FILE also carries the pre-1.1.0 title, which deposited files being frozen made uncorrectable; see release/RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md."
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24290698"
    description: "Version DOI of v1.0.0. It has no cpad_status / cpad_basis / cpad_checked columns and therefore cannot tell a reader which rows are training-set contaminated. Do not use it in preference to a later version."
date-released: 2026-11-18
# THE DOI IS NOT YET RESERVED FOR v1.2.0, AND THE ORDER MATTERS.
# RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md requires: reserve -> write the number into this file and into
# release/DATA_DESCRIPTOR.md -> upload -> publish. Not publish-then-patch, because
# deposited files are FROZEN: a DOI added afterwards reaches the repository copy only
# and leaves the deposited copy permanently inconsistent. That is what happened to
# v1.0.0's DATA_DESCRIPTOR.md.
#
# Replace the placeholder below with the number Zenodo reserves for the v1.2.0 draft,
# then run `python3 scripts/preflight_deposit.py`, which refuses while it is present.
#
# CONDITION ON A RESERVED DOI: it belongs to ONE draft. If that draft is discarded
# rather than published, Zenodo reserves a DIFFERENT number for the next attempt and
# this line and the descriptor must both be updated again.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24342313"
